@startuml

title One wake: firing the jobs whose occurrence has arrived

start

:sleep until the earliest next occurrence\namong the jobs held;

if (the sleep reached its bound,\nor the wall clock moved?) then (yes)
    :derive the earliest occurrence again\nfrom the current wall clock;
endif

if (a job definition changed?) then (yes)
    :re-read the job set,\nand re-arm the timer;
endif

:fire each job whose occurrence has arrived;

:recompute each fired job's next occurrence;

note right
    A job that is not due costs nothing:
    its next occurrence was computed when
    it entered the set or when it last fired.
end note

stop

@enduml
